content.text:
Team1 carrier idx3 is at (26,28) — the top-left corner! He's stuck at the boundary. Team1 attacks bottom, but the carrier has driven to the top-left corner instead of toward the bottom hoop. Why?

`aiCarrier` target calculation:
```js
const dirToHoop = norm(hoop.x - p.pos.x, hoop.y - p.pos.y);
let target = { x: hoop.x + dirToHoop.x * 0, y: hoop.y + (p.team === 0 ? 88 : -88) };
target.x += Math.sin(...) * 38;
if (nd < 56 && nearest) {
  const away = norm(p.pos.x - nearest.pos.x, p.pos.y - nearest.pos.y);
  target.x = p.pos.x + away.x * 70 + dirToHoop.x * 35;
  target.y = p.pos.y + away.y * 70 + dirToHoop.y * 35;
}
```
For team1, hoop=bottom (300,808), target y=720. That's fine. But the carrier is at (26,28) top-left. That means he moved away from the hoop due to the pressure avoidance branch. If a defender is near, `away` is from defender to carrier; if the defender is below/right of him, away points up-left, moving him to the corner. This can push him into the corner. Also, `dirToHoop` points down, but the away vector can dominate. Once at the corner, a defender follows, and away keeps pushing him into the corner; he gets stuck.

Additionally, team1's carrier at (26,28) is at the top-left corner, and his teammates are near bottom (offense spots), while team0 defenders are scattered. The carrier has been stuck for 25s. This is a pathing bug.

Fix AI carrier movement:
- Don't use a pure "away from defender" target that can point backward. Instead, blend mostly toward hoop with a sideways strafe perpendicular to the direction to the hoop. Choose the side away from defender.
- Clamp target within court.
- If in the corner, force toward center/hoop.

Better:
```js
const toHoop = norm(hoop.x - p.pos.x, hoop.y - p.pos.y);
const perp = {x:-toHoop.y, y:toHoop.x};
let side = Math.sign((nearest.pos.x-p.pos.x)*perp.x + (nearest.pos.y-p.pos.y)*perp.y) || 1;
let target = {x: p.pos.x + toHoop.x*100 + perp.x*side*45, y: ...};
if (d < 120) target = hoop-ish;
```
This always progresses toward the hoop while sidestepping. Also avoid corner by clamping target x 60..W-60, y 60..H-60.

For team1, toHoop points down; perp = (-1,0) etc. Good.

Also the AI carrier's shot logic didn't trigger because he was d~780 from hoop, so no shot, and passing only when d>300 and pressured (true), with 0.3 chance every 0.3-0.75s; he should pass. But maybe the pass target selection returned himself? No, mates only. Yet no passes in the 120s simulation (c.pass 0), which is odd. Wait, in the 120s sim with monkey patch, c.pass was 0. But in this 25s sim (without patch), maybe passes happened. The carrier at corner with teammates; if pressured, should pass with 0.3. Why not? `p.passCd` maybe >0? It decrements. Hmm.

Maybe the AI carrier isn't being updated at all because `updateAI` calls `aiCarrier`, which moves him to corner. The timer decrements, so decisions happen. But pass condition requires `pressured` (nd<50). At the corner, nearest defender may be far (team0 players at 485,642 etc.), so not pressured, no pass. And wantShot false (d>330), so he just drives... but the drive target is corner due to the old avoidance? Wait, if nd >= 56, target = (300,720), so he should move toward bottom. But he's at corner. That means at the time he reached the corner, he was pressured by a defender, and the away vector pushed him there; then the defender may have moved away, and he should head back to (300,720). But he's still at (26,28) after 25s. Could be because the target calculation with `dirToHoop.x*0` sets target.x = hoop.x = 300 plus sin*38, so x~300, y=720. He should move diagonally down-right. Unless he's stuck against the boundary due to separation with a defender, but the defender is far.

Wait, maybe team1 carrier is not moving because `p.stun > 0`? stun 0. Or `updateAI` isn't called for team1 carrier because `carrier === p` and aiCarrier is called; yes.

Hmm, the position (26,28) is exactly the clamp corner (x min 26, y min 28). This is suspicious: the AI target might be outside the court top-left, and movement pushes him there. The old avoidance target can be outside, but after reaching corner, target should change.

Could `hoop` be wrong? `attackHoop(team)` returns `team === 0 ? TOP_HOOP : BOTTOM_HOOP`. For team1 -> BOTTOM_HOOP (300,808). Yes.

But what if `p.team` is 0 for this player? The carrier object says t1. Good.

Maybe the AI carrier is being pushed by separation continuously by a team0 player who is also at the corner? Team0 idx3 is at (43,79), near the corner! So team1 carrier at (26,28) and team0 idx3 at (43,79) are 53 apart, just outside separation. Team0 idx3 is defending/pressuring him. Why is team0 idx3 at the corner? Team0 is defending its own hoop (bottom), but idx3 is at the top-left, far from its hoop. This is the "mark" defense: team0 defenders mark team1 opponents. Team1 carrier at corner; team0 idx3 marks an opponent? `aiDefense` for team0: closest AI defender pressures carrier (target 54 from carrier toward own hoop). The closest could be idx3, target near carrier + direction to own hoop (down) *54 = (26,82). So idx3 is at (43,79), pressuring. That keeps the carrier "pressured" (distance 53 > 50? Actually nd=53, not pressured for pass; but avoidance condition nd<56 triggers, so away vector from idx3 to carrier points up-left, pushing carrier into the corner). Yes! The avoidance condition is nd<56, while pressure for decisions is nd<50. The carrier is at distance 53, so he avoids into the corner but doesn't pass/shoot. Infinite corner trap.

Fix the avoidance: use sidestep toward hoop, not away; and clamp. Also maybe allow pass when nd<65 and d>300. Then he'd pass out of the trap.

Let's rewrite aiCarrier movement:

```js
const toHoop = norm(hoop.x-p.pos.x, hoop.y-p.pos.y);
const perp = {x:-toHoop.y, y:toHoop.x};
let strafe = 0;
if (nd < 70 && nearest) {
  const rel = (nearest.pos.x-p.pos.x)*perp.x + (nearest.pos.y-p.pos.y)*perp.y;
  strafe = rel > 0 ? -1 : 1; // move to the side opposite the defender
}
let target = { x: p.pos.x + toHoop.x*120 + perp.x*strafe*55, y: p.pos.y + toHoop.y*120 + perp.y*strafe*55 };
if (d < 130) target = {x: hoop.x + rand(-30,30), y: hoop.y + (team===0?70:-70)};
target.x = clamp(target.x, 55, W-55);
target.y = clamp(target.y, 55, H-55);
```
This ensures progress toward hoop. When d<130, go near hoop.

Also pass condition: `if (pressured && d > 280 && p.passCd <=0 && Math.random()<0.4)`. Use nd<65.

Also allow AI to shoot when d<330; at corner d~780, no. He will drive out.

Additionally, if an AI carrier has been in the same area for too long (stuck), force pass. Track `p.stuckTimer`? Could add: if speed < 20 for >1s and d>330, pass. But the new movement should avoid.

